# OPERATOR STATE. `make pi-ship` does not overwrite the copy on the
# Pi (PI_OWNED in the Makefile). The version in git is only the seed
# for a fresh install, and it will drift from the running one.
# Edit it on the Pi (`sudo pf tui`, House lists, a/d), then apply.
#
# Your own secure-DNS endpoints that the house segment may use while
# HOUSE_PRIVATE_DNS=on: <profile>.dns.<provider>.<tld>, never a bare
# provider. The house resolver answers each one with the first address in
# house_private_dns.ips, and sinkholes its parent zone. Thus no other
# profile of that provider resolves here. Off, or empty: inert.
#abcd1234xyz.dns.controld.com
